  "pin_notes": [
    "legacy board.ini sets -DPIN_SPARETEMP=PA3, but the legacy OPF code only read PIN_SPARETEMP1/PIN_SPARETEMP2, so PA3 (grey C7, 'Analog Inputs 7') was never assigned. Kept unassigned here (pinSpareTemp2 = unused); probably meant PIN_SPARETEMP2=PA3. pinSpareTemp* are 'future use' in Speeduino, so no functional effect today.",
    "readme lists Low Side 10 (PD15) and Low Side 11 (PG2), HALL inputs PG1/PE7/PE8/PE9 and digital inputs D2-D5; they are not mapped to any Speeduino function by default (same as legacy). They can still be chosen in TunerStudio for programmable outputs/inputs.",
    "upstream initialiseAll() drives LED_BUILTIN (PF10 on the black_f407zg variant) as an output and polls USER_BTN (PE4) as the EEPROM-reset key at boot; neither is in the core48 pin map, verify PE4 is not pulled low on the PCB."
  ]
